# Copy to backend/.env (same folder as mvnw.cmd). Never commit .env.
# The app also auto-loads backend/.env when you start Java from the repo root (IDE default working dir).

# Required for MongoDB resources API
MONGODB_USERNAME=duminduakhila2003_db_user
MONGODB_PASSWORD=Smart_campus1234
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://duminduakhila2003_db_user:Smart_campus1234@cluster0.1bxbmny.mongodb.net/smart_campus?retryWrites=true&w=majority

# Optional: use local MySQL instead of embedded H2 for JPA (contact + activity tables)
# SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=mysql
# SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/smart_campus_db
# SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME=your_mysql_user
# SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD=your_mysql_password

# Optional: Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD) OAuth2 login
#
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID must be the Application (client) ID — a UUID from Azure, for example:
#   MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890
# Do NOT use placeholder text like "local microsoft client id" (that is why login fails).
#
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET = a secret VALUE from "Certificates & secrets", not the secret's display name.
#
# New app registration (Azure Portal → Microsoft Entra ID → App registrations → New registration):
#   - Supported account types: choose "Accounts in any organizational directory and personal Microsoft accounts"
#     if you need @outlook.com / @live.com. Single-tenant "work/school only" causes "not enabled for consumers".
#   - Authentication → Add platform "Web" → Redirect URI (exact):
#       http://localhost:8081/login/oauth2/code/microsoft
#     (change host/port if your backend is not 8081.)
#
# MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID=common          # optional; see below
# FRONTEND_OAUTH_SUCCESS_URL=http://localhost:5173/login
#
# Microsoft login — error → සාමාන්‍ය හේතුව (quick reference)
#   ලක්ෂණය                         සාමාන්‍ය හේතුව
#   client does not exist          වැරදි client id, හෝ .env load නොවී placeholder යයි
#   not enabled for consumers      App එක personal accounts සඳහා configure නොවී / tenant common vs consumers mismatch
#
# --- If you see: "not enabled for consumers" / unauthorized_client ---
# Your app is probably "single tenant" or "work/school only". Fix in Azure Portal:
#   App registrations → your app → Authentication (or Manifest): allow personal accounts.
# When creating the app, pick: "Accounts in any organizational directory and personal Microsoft accounts".
# If the app is "Personal Microsoft accounts only", set in .env:
#   MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID=consumers
# If only campus/work accounts: use MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID=organizations or your tenant GUID; sign in with that account type only.
# Docs: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/quickstart-register-app

# Optional: Google OAuth2 login
#
# If Google shows "Error 401: invalid_client" / "The OAuth client was not found":
#   - GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID is wrong, truncated, or still a placeholder — paste the full Client ID from Google Cloud Console.
#   - Use OAuth client type "Web application" (not Desktop / iOS / Android only).
#   - Restart the backend after editing backend/.env.
#
# Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID:
#   - Application type: Web application
#   - Authorized redirect URIs (exact; backend port must match server.port, default 8081):
#       http://localhost:8081/login/oauth2/code/google
#   - Copy Client ID and Client secret into backend/.env (same folder as mvnw.cmd).
#
# Never use ellipsis (...) in .env — Google will return Error 401 invalid_client ("OAuth client was not found").
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=123456789-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# FRONTEND_OAUTH_SUCCESS_URL=http://localhost:5173/login

# Optional: comma-separated emails that skip the "pending approval" step (e.g. first campus administrator).
# APP_AUTH_AUTO_APPROVE_EMAILS=you@campus.edu

# Optional: first administrator (only if MongoDB has no active ADMINISTRATOR yet). Remove password after first login.
# BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@mycampus.edu
# BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=choose-a-strong-password
